acancy ID:</b> 188008 | <b>Closing date:</b> Monday 24 August, 2026, 12:00pm (UK time)</p>\n</div>\n<div class="down-button large-circle">\n<div class="stroke-container">\n<div class="vertical-stroke"></div>\n<div class="horizontal-stroke"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class="accordion-row-text">\n<p></p>\n<h3>Details</h3>\n<p><b>Grade:</b> Grade 6RS: £35,681 - £41,636 per annum pro rata</p>\n<div>The Oxford Internet Institute (OII) is a multidisciplinary research and teaching department at the University of Oxford, dedicated to exploring the implications of emerging technologies for how people live, work and govern.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Dr Ekaterina Hertog is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Research Assistant to support a quantitative component of the research project on Digital Lives of Care-Experienced Children in the UK.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>The RA will play a central role in identifying relevant variables across survey waves and supporting the construction of analytical datasets and descriptive outputs in Stata. The role involves a high degree of initiative and the ability to communicate effectively with data service providers and university library services.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>The position is variable hours, an average of 16 hours per week and fixed term until 31 December 2026. You will be based in Oxford but there may be the opportunity for occasional remote working.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>The ideal candidate will hold a doctoral degree or be a current doctoral student in a social science discipline, such as Sociology or Social Policy, Demography, Economics, or related discipline with quantitative research experience. They will have excellent written, verbal and data presentation skills.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Please contact OII Recruitment (recruit@oii.ox.ac.uk) with any queries relating to this vacancy.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>You will be required to upload a supporting statement, setting out how you meet the selection criteria, curriculum vitae and the names and contact details of two referees as part of your online application.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Only applications received online before noon UK TIME on 25 August 2026 can be considered.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>We cannot accept late applications due to time constraints.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div>Interviews are currently due to take place on 7 or 8 September 2026.</div>\n<div></div>\n<div><strong>Committed to equality and valuing diversity</strong></div>\n<div class="button-container-full-width">\n<button class="pseudo-button extend-button" onclick="window.location.href=\'https://www.oii.ox.ac.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/188008-Hertog-VH-G6-Nuffield.pdf\'">Download job pack\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class="extend_button">\n\n</span>\n</button>\n</div>\n<h3>How to apply</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Opening date:</b> Monday 3 August, 2026, 10:00am</li>\n<li><b>Closing date:</b> Monday 24 August, 2026, 12:00pm (UK time)</li>\n<li><b>Interview date:</b> Interviews are scheduled for the week beginning Monday 7 September, 2026</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Only applications received before 12:00pm  on Monday 24 August 2026 will be considered.</strong></p>\n<div class="button-container-full-width">\n<button class="pseudo-button extend-button" onclick="window.location.href=\'https://my.corehr.com/pls/uoxrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.display_form?p_company=10&amp;p_internal_external=E&amp;p_display_in_irish=N&amp;p_process_type=&amp;p_applicant_no=&amp;p_form_profile_detail=&amp;p_display_apply_ind=Y&amp;p_refresh_search=Y&amp;p_recruitment_id=188008\'">Apply now\n\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<span class="extend_button">\n\n</span>\n</button>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</main>'}], 'model': 'claude-haiku-4-5'}}
