2026-08-17 09:47:33,619 [DEBUG] anthropic._base_client: Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'headers': {'anthropic-user-profile-id': <anthropic.Omit object at 0x7fd43c166ea0>}, 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-02f0d50a-a2c8-482c-98c0-2562f39155ce', 'content': None, 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Extract all job/position listings from this career page HTML.\nReturn a JSON array where each element has:\n- "title": job title string\n- "url": full URL to the job posting (resolve relative URLs against https://www.oxfordmartin.ox.ac.uk/vacancies/)\n- "location": location if mentioned, else null\n- "role_type": "Full-time", "Part-time", "Fellowship", "Internship", or null\n\nOnly include actual job openings, internships, and fellowships.\nIgnore navigation links, news articles, blog posts, event listings, etc.\nIf there are no job listings on the page, return an empty array: []\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no other text.\n\n---\n\n<main>\n<section class="strip header-strip large-header light-header light-overlay" data-image-src="https://oms-www.transforms.svdcdn.com/production/images/140527_OMS_CENTRAL_08.jpg?w=1400&amp;h=600&amp;q=90&amp;auto=format&amp;fit=crop&amp;dm=1559554253&amp;s=c697a6c5c1ca6c90c5417c709ccd09fb" data-parallax="scroll">\n<div class="container">\n<div class="col col1of2">\n<h1>Vacancies</h1>\n</div>\n</div></section>\n<section class="strip nav-strip background-light-grey">\n\n</section>\n<section class="strip content-strip">\n<div class="container">\n<div class="row">\n<div class="col col2of3">\n<h4>Events and Venue Assistant</h4>\n<p><strong>Grade 5 £32,108- £37, 338 per annum</strong></p>\n<div>\n<a class="button light-button" href="https://bit.ly/4fR9PNM" target="_blank">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t More Information &amp; Apply\n\t\t\t\t\t  \n</a>\n</div>\n<p>We have an exciting opportunity to join the Oxford Martin School as our Events and Venue Assistant, working at the beautiful OMS building in Broad Street.</p><p>The Events and Venue Assistant provides support to our Events and Venue Manager in delivering our events programme and the use of the School’s building as a venue. Our events programme is pivotal to the mission and public reputation of the Oxford Martin School and this role will provide the support needed to ensure a successful, well-run events programme.<br/><br/>The post holder will support a variety of tasks to assist the Events and Venue Manager to include the set up and running of events including filming and live streaming; promotion of events in order to maximise attendance levels; maintaining an accurate database of event attendees; managing the room booking process for both internal and external bookings, updating the events section of the School’s website, and producing and sending the events newsletter.</p><p>Applications are made through our online recruitment portal using the link above. You will be asked to upload a CV and a supporting statement. The supporting statement must explain how you meet each of the selection criteria for the post using examples of your skills and experience.\xa0</p><p>Only applications received before 12:00 noon (UK time) on the 4th August can be considered. We expect to hold interviews on the 20th August 2026, in person at the office.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h4>Director, Global Governance and Strategic Engagement</h4>\n<p><strong>Standard Grade 10: Competitive Salary</strong></p>\n<div>\n<a class="button light-button" href="https://my.corehr.com/pls/uoxrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.display_form?p_company=10&amp;p_internal_external=E&amp;p_display_in_irish=N&amp;p_process_type=&amp;p_applicant_no=&amp;p_form_profile_detail=&amp;p_display_apply_ind=Y&amp;p_refresh_search=Y&amp;p_recruitment_id=187435" target="_blank">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t More Information &amp; Apply\n\t\t\t\t\t  \n</a>\n</div>\n<p>The Security Futures Lab, hosted by the Oxford Martin School, University of Oxford, was established to do one thing: rethink how security is understood and governed in an age of cascading, systemic risk.</p><p>We are looking for a Director, Global Governance &amp; Strategic Engagement to join our global leadership team — helping to build a pioneering international platform that bridges frontier research, multilateral institutions and public audiences across five continents.</p><p>We are seeking an exceptional senior leader to help redefine global debate on security, governance and institutional resilience at a moment of profound international change. In this high-profile role, you will translate cutting-edge research into policy action, governance innovation and public engagement.</p><p>You will lead engagement with governments, parliaments, multilateral institutions, civil society, media and public audiences, while driving the Lab’s international convening programme, including the Oxford Dialogues on Security and Futures.</p><p>Working closely with eight institutional partners across five continents, you will play a central role in building a new global platform for security cooperation and in democratising security by making complex ideas accessible, engaging wider publics, and enabling broader participation in rethinking national security strategies for the twenty-first century.</p><p>As the senior operational lead within the three-person leadership team, you will also oversee day-to-day management, financial stewardship and administrative coordination across a complex and ambitious international programme.</p><p>This is a rare opportunity to help build a globally significant initiative from the ground up — combining intellectual leadership, international engagement and institution-building at one of the world’s leading universities.</p><p>The post is fixed term for 30 months.</p><p>Only applications received before 12:00 noon (BST) on 27th July 2026 can be considered. We expect to hold interviews around the 4th August 2026.</p>\n<hr/>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</section>\n</main>'}], 'model': 'claude-haiku-4-5'}}
